# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Watchtower environment variables (TEMPLATE — safe to commit).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values there. `.env` is git-ignored.
#   pwsh:   Copy-Item .env.example .env
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Database: Neon Postgres (provisioned via Vercel → Storage) -------------
# Find both strings in Neon's "Connect" widget
# (Vercel → your project → Storage → the database → Connect):
#
#   DATABASE_URL          = the POOLED string. Its host contains "-pooler".
#                           Used by the app/serverless at runtime.
#   DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED = the direct (non-pooling) string. No "-pooler".
#                           Used by Prisma for migrations. This is the name
#                           Vercel's Neon integration injects automatically.
#
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# --- TMDB (film & TV watches) ----------------------------------------------
# TMDB issues two credentials. Only the read access token is needed here: it is
# the v4 style and travels in an Authorization header, so it never ends up in a
# URL, a log line or a referrer the way the v3 api_key query parameter does.
# Copy the long "API Read Access Token" from
#   themoviedb.org -> Settings -> API
# The engine polls from Vercel, so this must also be set there (and Vercel
# needs a redeploy afterwards):
#   - Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables -> TMDB_ACCESS_TOKEN
# TMDB is free for non-commercial use and requires attribution.
TMDB_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- Cron auth --------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared secret so only our scheduler can trigger /api/cron/poll. Polling is
# driven by the GitHub Actions workflow .github/workflows/poll-watches.yml
# (Vercel's Hobby plan only allows once-daily crons), so the same value must be
# set in BOTH places, and Vercel needs a redeploy after any change:
#   - Vercel   -> Settings -> Environment Variables -> CRON_SECRET
#   - GitHub   -> repo Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> CRON_SECRET
# Leave unset locally: the route allows unauthenticated calls when it is absent.
# Generate:  openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=
